00:18:53.510 --> 00:18:56.750
- Oh, so it's you that lives next door.

00:18:56.750 --> 00:18:59.170
- Yes, would you like to dispossess me?

00:18:59.170 --> 00:19:00.000
- Woman, go back.

00:19:00.120 --> 00:19:01.000
to your pig pen

00:19:01.000 --> 00:19:01.640
where you belong.

00:19:01.820 --> 00:19:02.380
Uh-huh.

00:19:02.620 --> 00:19:03.620
You've been snooping

00:19:03.620 --> 00:19:04.700
around my cottage.

00:19:05.200 --> 00:19:06.260
Listen here, young man.

00:19:06.300 --> 00:19:07.060
If I catch you

00:19:07.060 --> 00:19:08.240
hanging around there again,

00:19:08.340 --> 00:19:08.920
Mama certainly

00:19:08.920 --> 00:19:09.920
is going to whip Papa.

00:19:10.400 --> 00:19:10.540
What?

00:19:11.040 --> 00:19:12.290
Say, what ails you?

00:19:12.350 --> 00:19:13.070
Are you reducing?

00:19:13.630 --> 00:19:14.390
You see,

00:19:14.610 --> 00:19:15.810
this is my Uncle Claude.

00:19:16.310 --> 00:19:17.250
I've spoken to you

00:19:17.250 --> 00:19:17.930
about him often.

00:19:18.490 --> 00:19:19.370
Mr. Davis,

00:19:19.510 --> 00:19:20.470
president of the

00:19:20.470 --> 00:19:21.330
International Ketchup

00:19:21.330 --> 00:19:22.650
and Tomato Company.

00:19:23.740 --> 00:19:24.740
Gee, I'm sorry.

00:19:24.780 --> 00:19:25.420
Oh, woman,

00:19:25.600 --> 00:19:26.780
will you leave?

00:19:26.990 --> 00:19:27.810
Oh, Uncle Claude,

00:19:27.890 --> 00:19:28.430
can you ever,

00:19:28.730 --> 00:19:30.000
will you have your,

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:33.520
If my husband had only told me.

00:19:33.520 --> 00:19:35.320
Tom, why didn't you?

00:19:35.320 --> 00:19:40.310
You see, Uncle Claude, her husband is a friend of yours.

00:19:40.310 --> 00:19:45.320
He's a big tomato sauce man from... from...

00:19:45.320 --> 00:19:46.820
What are you raving about?

00:19:46.820 --> 00:19:49.320
You're not a big tomato and sauce man from...

00:19:49.320 --> 00:19:52.460
Oh, Uncle Claude, I'm so sorry.

00:19:52.460 --> 00:19:54.960
Oh, hold on. I'm gonna get out of here.

00:19:54.960 --> 00:19:55.960
I'm gonna get out of here.

00:19:55.960 --> 00:19:58.410
Now, now, now. You mustn't get hurt.

00:19:58.410 --> 00:20:00.000
Would you take the air?

00:20:08.760 --> 00:20:21.090
back in a minute. I'm sorry, but I've got to be going. My dear, take my advice and don't

00:20:21.090 --> 00:20:30.000
become too intimate with that terrible woman. If Tom had ever married a creature like that...

00:20:40.560 --> 00:20:42.840
Now what's this all about? What did you do to him?

00:20:42.840 --> 00:20:45.990
He didn't have the slightest idea who he was.

00:20:45.990 --> 00:20:48.600
I only knew him to be one of those rich new arrivals.

00:20:48.600 --> 00:20:54.210
So I went up into his suite and I pulled some of that high-pressure sales method of mine on him.

00:20:54.210 --> 00:20:57.080
Good night. You fixed my future now.

00:20:57.080 --> 00:20:59.920
I'm sorry. Dreadfully sorry.

00:21:00.600 --> 00:21:06.270
I knew you'd keep on clowning like this till something happened.

00:21:06.270 --> 00:21:10.720
Tom, honestly, I wouldn't have had this happen for anything in the world.

00:21:10.720 --> 00:21:12.020
Stop acting.

00:21:12.020 --> 00:21:17.000
You're getting all set now to pull that one about the millionaire feeling sorry for the tramp.

00:21:17.000 --> 00:21:18.000
No, no, don't.

00:21:18.000 --> 00:21:20.000
No, I should have quit you long ago.

00:21:20.000 --> 00:21:24.800
Anyway, before this thing happened, I'm through.

00:21:31.560 --> 00:21:33.300
- Thank you, my dear, thank you.

00:21:33.300 --> 00:21:37.000
I'm so glad that Tom married a nice little girl like you.

00:21:37.000 --> 00:21:38.920
I'm gonna like you very much, my dear.

00:21:38.920 --> 00:21:41.920
And when Uncle Claude says he likes,

00:21:41.920 --> 00:21:43.200
he says it with cash.

00:21:43.200 --> 00:21:45.240
Bye, my son.

00:21:45.240 --> 00:21:46.080
- Bye.

00:21:46.080 --> 00:21:55.000
- Goodbye, Uncle Claude.

00:21:55.000 --> 00:21:56.310
- Come away from that woman.

00:22:03.260 --> 00:22:05.220
- Leaving so soon, Uncle? - Yeah, yeah.

00:22:05.220 --> 00:22:06.860
Well, I'll walk part of the ways with you.

00:22:06.860 --> 00:22:08.130
Look here, Tom.

00:22:08.130 --> 00:22:11.470
If you had ever married a woman like that tall creature,

00:22:11.470 --> 00:22:13.690
you'd never get a cent of my money.

00:22:13.690 --> 00:22:16.870
Well, being married to her would be hard on me, wouldn't it?

00:22:16.870 --> 00:22:20.380
Hard? It'd be fatal to you or anybody else.

00:22:20.380 --> 00:22:23.850
I'll walk to the pier with you.

00:22:23.850 --> 00:22:28.290
It isn't very polite to start reading the minute you're home.

00:22:28.290 --> 00:22:30.000
I'm trying to find a little good news.

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:31.720
It was a nice murder or something.

00:22:31.720 --> 00:22:34.720
A little comedy relief for the home fire blues you sing.

00:22:37.600 --> 00:22:40.540
Stop hiding behind that paper.

00:22:40.540 --> 00:22:42.870
Hiding from you? Impossible.

00:22:42.870 --> 00:22:46.940
I told you when I married you that I couldn't cook and I don't like housework.

00:22:46.940 --> 00:22:49.340
Yeah, well, I found that out. You're just lazy.

00:22:49.340 --> 00:22:50.710
Lazy? I am not.

00:22:50.710 --> 00:22:53.890
I'd work like a dog if I had something artistic to do.

00:22:53.890 --> 00:22:58.190
Something befitting a delicate, high-strung, sensitive personality like mine.

00:22:58.190 --> 00:23:00.000
Sensitive? Ha ha!

00:23:00.640 --> 00:23:02.180
- That's sensitive, ha ha!

00:23:02.180 --> 00:23:04.540
- If I could bob my hair and put a bandeau around it

00:23:04.540 --> 00:23:06.340
and a couple of yards of cheese cloth around here

00:23:06.340 --> 00:23:08.000
and go in for Greek dancing.

00:23:08.000 --> 00:23:10.280
- Yeah, well, suppose you start expressing yourself

00:23:10.280 --> 00:23:12.920
by putting on an apron and buying some frankfurters

00:23:12.920 --> 00:23:14.620
and doing a little Greek cooking.

00:23:14.620 --> 00:23:15.740
- Are you broadcasting?

00:23:15.740 --> 00:23:16.920
I'm listening.

00:23:16.920 --> 00:23:19.670
- Well, I warn you, I'll leave you.

00:23:19.670 --> 00:23:20.930
What I need is the kind of a life

00:23:20.930 --> 00:23:23.590
that will bring back my radio voice.

00:23:23.590 --> 00:23:26.770
Plenty of rest and good food and regularity of--

00:23:26.770 --> 00:23:29.700
- Yes, fresh air and long walks and sunshine.

00:23:30.410 --> 00:23:33.690
You don't want a wife, you want a sanitarium.

00:23:41.750 --> 00:23:54.160
Try talking to your wife occasionally.

00:23:54.160 --> 00:23:56.110
When, during intermission?

00:23:56.110 --> 00:24:00.000
Oh, why did I ever...

00:24:00.250 --> 00:24:05.180
For revenge, I guess, and maybe you sure got it.

00:24:05.180 --> 00:24:06.930
Oh!

00:24:06.930 --> 00:24:17.260
What a good cook, Grace, is, and I'll knock you right through that door into her pots and pans.

00:24:17.260 --> 00:24:20.260
You should have married a kitchen stove.

00:24:20.260 --> 00:24:21.420
That's hot.

00:24:21.420 --> 00:24:24.440
No more wisecracks from the broken crockery.

00:24:24.440 --> 00:24:27.440
Say, I wisecrack just as much as I want.

00:24:27.440 --> 00:24:28.680
Do what?

00:24:28.680 --> 00:24:29.540
Come on, get out of here.

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:31.400
Slam the door as you go out.

00:24:46.620 --> 00:24:49.290
You look worried.

00:24:52.610 --> 00:24:53.960
I'm not worried.

00:24:54.370 --> 00:24:55.570
I'm just exhausted.

00:24:56.820 --> 00:24:58.450
Lettie and I just had another battle.

00:25:03.360 --> 00:25:08.490
You know, Grace, my wife doesn't understand me.

00:25:08.490 --> 00:25:11.000
That's a shame.

00:25:11.000 --> 00:25:15.140
If I was only married to someone like you, Grace, dear.

00:25:15.140 --> 00:25:21.270
Tommy.

00:25:21.270 --> 00:25:25.280
Did anybody ever tell you you had lovely hands?

00:25:25.280 --> 00:25:27.650
Since I've been married.

00:25:34.350 --> 00:25:36.390
I didn't know you were home, Harry.

00:25:36.650 --> 00:25:38.610
Yeah, I'll send you a telegram the next time.

00:25:45.060 --> 00:25:46.960
Do you suppose he saw us holding hands?

00:25:47.330 --> 00:25:48.080
I don't know.

00:25:48.540 --> 00:25:50.170
And I don't care if he did.

00:25:50.800 --> 00:25:51.580
The brute.

00:26:02.810 --> 00:26:04.370
- Come in.

00:26:04.370 --> 00:26:05.290
- Hello, Harry.

00:26:05.290 --> 00:26:06.470
- Pull down the drawbridge and enter.

00:26:06.470 --> 00:26:08.230
The Duke's away on a hunting trip.

00:26:08.230 --> 00:26:12.290
- Huh, sit down.

00:26:12.290 --> 00:26:14.210
- Would you believe me if I said

00:26:14.210 --> 00:26:16.420
that my wife didn't understand me?

00:26:16.420 --> 00:26:17.660
- Oh, that's too bad.

00:26:17.660 --> 00:26:18.760
Why don't you stay home nights

00:26:18.760 --> 00:26:20.480
and tell her something about yourself?

00:26:20.480 --> 00:26:23.440
- No, if she spent half as much time on her face

00:26:23.440 --> 00:26:27.050
as she did her veal cutlet, well, I'd relish it.

00:26:27.050 --> 00:26:30.000
- Are you speaking of the lady or the cutlet?

00:26:30.000 --> 00:26:34.640
how I feel when I come home nights and find her looking like the follies of 1910? Takes

00:26:34.640 --> 00:26:40.580
all the pep out of me. Now, with you, Luddy, it's different. I, uh... Oh, Harry, you're

00:26:40.580 --> 00:26:47.360
killing me. Yeah, you're somewhat of a killer yourself. Harry, I wish Tommy'd get a suit

00:26:47.360 --> 00:26:53.130
like yours. Oh, you like this suit, huh? Soft, creepy material. Get the bear's suggestion

00:26:53.130 --> 00:27:00.000
of her. Figure. It's a lady shriek from London. It's a scream, all right. I like the little

00:27:00.000 --> 00:27:01.860
around the Majasbo here.

00:27:01.860 --> 00:27:03.220
It's really stunning.

00:27:03.220 --> 00:27:05.040
You know, Letty, you have beautiful,

00:27:05.040 --> 00:27:06.900
slender, graceful hands.

00:27:06.900 --> 00:27:08.330
You really think so?

00:27:08.330 --> 00:27:09.170
Yeah.

00:27:09.170 --> 00:27:11.110
Grace's hands are all thumbs.

00:27:11.110 --> 00:27:12.510
Mostly down.

00:27:12.510 --> 00:27:23.500
Harry, I'd like to speak to you outside a minute.

00:27:23.500 --> 00:27:25.190
All right, Tom.

00:27:36.940 --> 00:27:39.220
- What's the idea of making love to my wife?

00:27:39.220 --> 00:27:41.490
- That wasn't love, that was conversation.

00:27:41.490 --> 00:27:43.210
- Well, when you had to hold her hands,

00:27:43.210 --> 00:27:45.340
what were you describing, a wrestling match?

00:27:45.340 --> 00:27:47.170
- I'm a nervous temperament.

00:27:47.170 --> 00:27:48.530
- Well, you keep your nervous temperament

00:27:48.530 --> 00:27:49.710
away from my wife.

00:27:49.710 --> 00:27:51.560
- Yeah, where were you?

00:27:51.560 --> 00:27:55.630
- I was practicing boys' culture.

00:27:55.630 --> 00:28:00.000
- Well, since when is my home a rehearsal hall?

00:28:00.000 --> 00:28:01.840
- You wouldn't go home if you saw one.

00:28:01.840 --> 00:28:02.600
- Yeah?

00:28:02.600 --> 00:28:03.840
- Will you come on down by the ocean?

00:28:03.840 --> 00:28:05.000
I want to talk to you.

00:28:05.000 --> 00:28:06.400
- Yeah?

00:28:06.400 --> 00:28:17.590
- Yeah.

00:28:17.590 --> 00:28:27.150
- Sure.

00:28:27.150 --> 00:28:27.990
- Cat.

00:28:27.990 --> 00:28:30.000
- Grace, I am one jump ahead of a fit.

00:28:33.610 --> 00:28:38.930
- Plenty! - So sweaty! Calm yourself! Tell me what happened!

00:28:39.100 --> 00:28:43.730
Listen, Harry was in here a minute ago, and he was telling me what pretty hands I have.

00:28:43.770 --> 00:28:47.840
- Oh, really? - Mm-hmm. And Tommy got terribly jealous.

00:28:47.940 --> 00:28:50.640
Jealous? Tom, jealous of Harry?

00:28:50.710 --> 00:28:53.620
Oh, how perfectly ridiculous!

00:28:53.720 --> 00:28:58.040
Oh, I don't know about that. Tommy admires me very much.

00:28:58.080 --> 00:28:59.890
But listen here, from what I can gather...

00:29:00.350 --> 00:29:05.640
- Harry is extremely jealous of Tommy. - You don't say so.

00:29:06.670 --> 00:29:12.880
- Isn't that ridiculous? - Listen, were they really very angry?

00:29:12.880 --> 00:29:18.660
- Angry? They've gone down the beach now to have it out. - Oh, so they kill each other.

00:29:18.660 --> 00:29:24.250
- Boy, wouldn't that be awful? - Oh, and Harry's the only husband I've got.

00:29:24.250 --> 00:29:29.440
- Well, Tommy's no leading man, but believe me, he is a comfort around the house.

00:29:43.180 --> 00:29:44.640
- Are you all right, Tommy, darling?

00:29:44.640 --> 00:29:46.180
- Are you all right, dear?

00:29:46.180 --> 00:29:47.410
- Certainly we're all right.

00:29:47.410 --> 00:29:48.570
Aren't we, Tom?

00:29:48.570 --> 00:29:49.400
- Perfect.

00:29:49.400 --> 00:29:51.340
- Tom and I have just come to a big decision,

00:29:51.340 --> 00:29:52.180
haven't we, Tom?

00:29:52.180 --> 00:29:53.830
- Yes, indeed we have.

00:29:53.830 --> 00:29:54.870
- You tell 'em, Tom.

00:29:57.480 --> 00:29:59.410
- You tell 'em and I'll pat my foot.

00:30:00.320 --> 00:30:01.700
Well, you see, the fact is...

00:30:01.700 --> 00:30:03.100
Yes, it certainly is.

00:30:03.570 --> 00:30:04.750
Yes, it certainly is.

00:30:04.790 --> 00:30:05.290
What is it?

00:30:05.690 --> 00:30:06.350
A vaudeville act?

00:30:06.430 --> 00:30:07.170
Go ahead and spill it.

00:30:07.230 --> 00:30:08.350
Yes, let's have it.

00:30:08.600 --> 00:30:09.840
Well, to get right to the point,

00:30:10.260 --> 00:30:12.710
we, uh, we figured, uh,

00:30:12.870 --> 00:30:13.970
we'd exchange wives.

00:30:14.620 --> 00:30:15.560
Yes, precisely.

00:30:16.040 --> 00:30:16.480
What?

00:30:16.970 --> 00:30:18.450
Well, you're both crazy.

00:30:18.630 --> 00:30:21.230
Well, now, you see, Tom figured that Grace was such a good cook,

00:30:21.270 --> 00:30:22.970
and he's such a food hound that...

00:30:22.970 --> 00:30:24.920
Yes, and Harry figured that, that, uh,

00:30:24.920 --> 00:30:26.360
as long as he likes to make Whoopi,

00:30:26.680 --> 00:30:28.100
and, uh, Lettie invented it...

00:30:28.100 --> 00:30:30.000
Mm, so you two mastermind.

00:30:30.250 --> 00:30:32.350
that you had both married the wrong girl.

00:30:32.350 --> 00:30:34.350
- And you'd remedy the mistake by switching.

00:30:34.350 --> 00:30:35.750
- Well, that's about it.

00:30:35.750 --> 00:30:36.950
- That's exactly it.

00:30:36.950 --> 00:30:38.890
- Well, of all the gall.

00:30:38.890 --> 00:30:41.130
- They don't need a nerve tonic, that's a cinch.

00:30:41.130 --> 00:30:42.530
- Well, now understand, girls,

00:30:42.530 --> 00:30:44.270
we're not going to really--

00:30:44.270 --> 00:30:46.230
- Oh, no, we won't really--

00:30:46.230 --> 00:30:49.350
- Oh, you mean you won't, really?

00:30:49.350 --> 00:30:53.020
- Oh, you won't, really?

00:30:53.020 --> 00:30:53.770
- No.

00:30:53.770 --> 00:30:54.870
- Not really?

00:30:54.870 --> 00:30:55.810
- No, no.

00:30:55.810 --> 00:30:56.710
- I think--

00:30:56.710 --> 00:30:57.720
- Really?

00:30:57.720 --> 00:30:58.560
- I see.

00:30:58.560 --> 00:31:00.000
- So we girls have just taken on probation

00:31:00.000 --> 00:31:07.480
So you two fellows have figured it all out, and you're going to give us the air a refined air ozone

00:31:07.620 --> 00:31:13.040
Well, I think it's outrageous and disgusting whose idea was this anyway?

00:31:15.260 --> 00:31:17.160
Well, we thought that

00:31:17.160 --> 00:31:19.160
It was a kind of a collaboration

00:31:19.160 --> 00:31:22.120
Yeah, I wrote the words and he wrote the music

00:31:22.120 --> 00:31:25.000
Oh, I see it took two heads to hammer this idea

00:31:26.120 --> 00:31:29.670
Say grace step into my office, will you?

00:31:30.250 --> 00:31:31.600
We'll talk this thing over.

00:31:31.600 --> 00:31:40.430
- After all, you don't think we'd-- - Keep calm, keep calm.

00:31:40.430 --> 00:31:43.570
I know, but I've never swapped wives before, neither of you.

00:31:43.570 --> 00:31:47.440
- Keep cool, Tommy, keep cool. - I'm c-c-cool, all right.

00:31:47.440 --> 00:31:51.580
Now, Letty, you're not gonna really let them.

00:31:51.580 --> 00:31:53.920
Listen, can't you see? If they really want to get rid of us,

00:31:53.920 --> 00:31:55.940
we can't do anything else but let them?

00:31:55.940 --> 00:32:00.000
But supposing after we exchange for a while, Harry would prefer you...

00:32:01.180 --> 00:32:04.390
- Don't worry, I never purchase goods by sample.

00:32:04.390 --> 00:32:05.930
- Well, that's a relief.

00:32:05.930 --> 00:32:08.450
- Would you want Tommy as a permanent institution?

00:32:08.450 --> 00:32:10.250
- I should say not.

00:32:10.250 --> 00:32:13.610
- Well, I don't want that giraffe that belongs to you.

00:32:13.610 --> 00:32:16.360
- Well, well anyway, I'm afraid, oh I just couldn't.

00:32:16.360 --> 00:32:18.260
- Nonsense, this is the chance of a lifetime

00:32:18.260 --> 00:32:19.500
to teach them such a lesson

00:32:19.500 --> 00:32:21.660
that they'll eat out of our hands forever after.

00:32:21.660 --> 00:32:22.510
- How?

00:32:22.510 --> 00:32:24.350
- Listen, Tommy's always bawling me out

00:32:24.350 --> 00:32:26.350
about being a rotten cook and housekeeper.

00:32:26.350 --> 00:32:28.850
You take him for a week and stuff him with food

00:32:28.850 --> 00:32:30.000
'til he cries for help.

00:32:30.480 --> 00:32:31.820
That's not a bad idea.

00:32:31.820 --> 00:32:36.830
Harry's always bawling you out about not dressing well, sitting home and tending to the house.

00:32:36.830 --> 00:32:38.420
I'll take him for a week.

00:32:38.420 --> 00:32:40.390
Oh boy, how I'll take him.

00:32:40.390 --> 00:32:45.290
I'll give him so much excitement and action that he'll crawl back to you on his hands and knees.

00:32:45.290 --> 00:32:47.920
You're a genius.

00:32:47.920 --> 00:32:50.490
Oh, you're generous.

00:32:50.490 --> 00:32:51.480
What do you say?

00:32:51.480 --> 00:32:52.340
I'm with you.

00:32:52.340 --> 00:32:53.490
Okay, baby.

00:32:53.490 --> 00:32:56.440
Oh, this is gonna be sweet.

00:32:56.440 --> 00:32:57.910
Come on now.

00:33:04.960 --> 00:33:14.910
- Well, we've decided.

00:33:14.910 --> 00:33:16.760
You come over here with me for a week,

00:33:16.760 --> 00:33:21.520
and Tommy, you go over there with Grace.

00:33:21.520 --> 00:33:23.870
- You mean for a week?

00:33:23.870 --> 00:33:24.810
For a week?

00:33:24.810 --> 00:33:26.800
- We can get a divorce later.

00:33:26.800 --> 00:33:28.120
Grace and I are not gonna take any

00:33:28.120 --> 00:33:30.000
so serious steps as that until we're perfectly

00:33:30.000 --> 00:33:35.070
sure that she wants Tommy and I want you. And a week's trial will give us all the information

00:33:35.070 --> 00:33:44.310
