00:57:22.810 --> 00:57:23.810
He wasn't here, he wasn't.

00:57:23.810 --> 00:57:24.810
He wasn't?

00:57:24.810 --> 00:57:28.020
I suppose he isn't here now.

00:57:28.020 --> 00:57:30.000
You tell it to the judge.

00:57:30.410 --> 00:57:32.710
He just paid for listening to lies.

00:57:32.810 --> 00:57:34.680
Come on, boys, take him along.

00:57:34.890 --> 00:57:38.260
You can't arrest me. I've got an appointment for a facial tomorrow.

00:57:38.290 --> 00:57:39.750
So's your Aunt Emma.

00:57:39.850 --> 00:57:42.550
Oh, my Aunt Emma wouldn't know what a facial was.

00:57:42.650 --> 00:57:45.030
- This way out. - Oh, you make me sick.

00:57:45.130 --> 00:57:47.630
Come on, you sir. I don't belong here.

00:57:47.640 --> 00:57:56.650
Making to talk for the past half hour,

00:57:56.750 --> 00:58:00.000
kindly tell the court what you were doing at this barkeep.

00:58:00.350 --> 00:58:04.590
- Are you a singer too? - No, Your Honor. I am not a singer.

00:58:04.740 --> 00:58:09.090
I am Claude Davis, president of the International Tomato Patcher Company.

00:58:09.160 --> 00:58:11.880
Will you tell the truth about this, or will you go to jail?

00:58:11.920 --> 00:58:14.820
Your Honor, this may seem a bit strange to you,

00:58:14.920 --> 00:58:17.200
but we traded husbands and wives for a week.

00:58:17.300 --> 00:58:18.740
You did what?

00:58:18.920 --> 00:58:23.240
I am really married to Tommy Robbins, and she is really married to Harry Miller.

00:58:23.700 --> 00:58:25.800
Both boys got tired of their own wives and...

00:58:25.900 --> 00:58:30.000
Look here, Tom Robbins, do you mean to say that you are married to this...

00:58:30.030 --> 00:58:31.290
One moment, sir.

00:58:31.290 --> 00:58:33.710
Another remark like that, and you'll go to jail for a month.

00:58:33.710 --> 00:58:36.010
But my dear judge, it's been...

00:58:36.010 --> 00:58:37.770
That's all there is to it.

00:58:37.770 --> 00:58:39.570
Tommy preferred Grace to me,

00:58:39.570 --> 00:58:41.850
and Harry preferred me to Grace, so we swapped.

00:58:41.850 --> 00:58:43.570
Yeah, and your honor, I got no bargain.

00:58:43.570 --> 00:58:45.400
I regret it, so do I.

00:58:45.400 --> 00:58:47.130
No one regrets it more than I do.

00:58:47.130 --> 00:58:48.830
And I want Tommy back.

00:58:48.830 --> 00:58:50.620
He's not very much to look at, Judge,

00:58:50.620 --> 00:58:52.950
but he does lend atmosphere in the home.

00:58:52.950 --> 00:58:56.180
He lends more sphere than atmos, but I like it.

00:58:56.180 --> 00:59:00.000
Well, if I understand this situation correctly,

00:59:00.250 --> 00:59:05.340
All parties to this astonishing and illegal exchange

00:59:05.340 --> 00:59:08.490
sincerely regret it and desire it to return

00:59:08.490 --> 00:59:10.530
to their respective husbands and wives.

00:59:10.730 --> 00:59:11.850
Will you repeat that, Judge?

00:59:11.970 --> 00:59:14.770
Judge, my pal, I'd rather live with Scarlet Fever

00:59:14.770 --> 00:59:15.590
than with this woman.

00:59:16.170 --> 00:59:18.110
Me too, only I'll take tonsillitis.

00:59:18.600 --> 00:59:21.360
And I'd rather eat rat poison than live with that Mrs. Miller.

00:59:21.600 --> 00:59:22.740
You'll eat those words.

00:59:23.080 --> 00:59:25.520
He'll eat anything he can get near his mouth.

00:59:26.060 --> 00:59:27.800
And that's so big he can't miss it.

00:59:28.920 --> 00:59:30.000
Oh, and to say,

00:59:30.000 --> 00:59:32.980
I thought I was going to give you a big check.

00:59:32.980 --> 00:59:35.220
Very well then.

00:59:35.220 --> 00:59:37.470
I command that each one of you

00:59:37.470 --> 00:59:40.880
return immediately to his husband or wife.

00:59:40.880 --> 00:59:44.370
And to ensure good conduct in the future,

00:59:44.370 --> 00:59:46.770
I parole each husband to each wife

00:59:46.770 --> 00:59:49.010
and each wife to each husband.

00:59:49.010 --> 00:59:53.240
Your Honor, may I ask my nephew a question?

00:59:53.240 --> 00:59:54.160
Yes.

00:59:54.160 --> 01:00:00.000
Tom, how about my future grand-nephew or grand-niece?

01:00:00.000 --> 01:00:02.280
or whatever it was going to be.

01:00:02.610 --> 01:00:04.610
Answer the gentleman's question.

01:00:04.610 --> 01:00:08.010
Well, you see, Mr. Davis, Your Honor,

01:00:08.010 --> 01:00:12.200
that little sweater I was knitting was for Hortense, my dog.

01:00:14.630 --> 01:00:15.690
How did you deceive her?

01:00:15.690 --> 01:00:16.990
Oh, I'll add...

01:00:16.990 --> 01:00:18.390
Now, Uncle Claude, don't you lose your...

01:00:18.390 --> 01:00:21.890
Now, look here, as for you, you will regret this to your dying days.

01:00:21.890 --> 01:00:23.850
You are a minister of society.

01:00:23.850 --> 01:00:25.550
Why, the world would be better off.

01:00:25.550 --> 01:00:28.850
Mr. Davis, I advise you to control your temper.

01:00:28.850 --> 01:00:30.000
Much, please.

01:00:30.030 --> 01:00:32.370
In the next case, oh dear.

01:00:42.440 --> 01:00:44.020
You take your hands off of me.

01:00:44.020 --> 01:00:45.810
Aren't you satisfied?

01:00:45.810 --> 01:00:47.940
Ruining my reputation?

01:00:47.940 --> 01:00:50.910
Breaking my faith in mankind?

01:00:50.910 --> 01:00:52.680
Yes, and womankind, too.

01:00:52.680 --> 01:00:54.760
But Uncle Claude, it's not as bad as you think.

01:00:54.760 --> 01:00:56.660
You haven't lost anything, I'm sorry.

01:00:56.660 --> 01:00:59.190
I'll give you back the check that you gave me.

01:01:00.730 --> 01:01:02.120
Say, where'd you get that check?

01:01:02.370 --> 01:01:04.270
I never gave that check to you.

01:01:04.370 --> 01:01:05.760
I gave it to Tom.

01:01:05.780 --> 01:01:08.190
Well, it was made out to Mr. and Mrs. Tom Robbins,

01:01:08.290 --> 01:01:10.180
so naturally it wasn't mine.

01:01:10.250 --> 01:01:13.860
Yes, and good husbands always share everything with their wives.

01:01:17.220 --> 01:01:21.490
The thing that you have taken from me that hurts more than anything else

01:01:21.840 --> 01:01:24.100
is the fond hope I had

01:01:24.160 --> 01:01:26.790
for a future grand-nephew,

01:01:27.680 --> 01:01:29.320
or a grand-need.

01:01:31.370 --> 01:01:38.860
If it wasn't for that, I might be able to forgive all of you.

01:01:38.860 --> 01:01:41.620
- Uncle Claude. - What do you want?

01:02:02.270 --> 01:02:10.320
He's a king, he's wined and dined us royally, and forgiven us everything.

01:02:12.020 --> 01:02:17.000
Given Ruth is promised that she can marry Joe, that's if she loves him 12 months hence,

01:02:17.080 --> 01:02:18.200
of course she will, I know.

01:02:19.120 --> 01:02:24.300
And Sally can have her parents to honor and obey, that's if in a year she still can stand

01:02:24.300 --> 01:02:25.340
to listen to him play.

01:02:26.400 --> 01:02:28.390
He gave grace back her husband.

01:02:31.980 --> 01:02:53.120
ladies and gentlemen nieces nephews and grandkids and now i have a surprise for letty i have taken

01:02:53.120 --> 01:03:00.000
sally and ruth abroad for a whole year and i want letty to come with us
